<h1>first-in, first-out</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A policy that items are processed in order of arrival.  A <a href="queue.html"><em>queue</em></a> implements this.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="lastfirstout.html"><em>last-in, first-out</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Same as <a href="firstcome.html"><em>first come, first served</em></a>.  A <a href="breadthfirst.html"><em>breadth-first search</em></a> checks newly encountered nodes first-in, first-out. Often written as FIFO.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

<hr>

